## GENERATE_FIBONACCI_SEQUENCE
- [IMPL-FIBONACCI_GENERATE_SEQUENCE] [ARCH-FIBONACCI_CLI_SCRIPT] [REQ-FIBONACCI_PRINT] How: Return the first count terms of the zero-based Fibonacci sequence as an integer list.
Contract:
  INPUT: count (integer)
  OUTPUT: sequence (list of integer)
  DATA: sequence (list of integer)
  PRE: count >= 0
  POST: length(sequence) == count; sequence[0] == 0 when count > 0; sequence[1] == 1 when count > 1; each later term is the sum of the previous two
  EFFECTS: Exn
  FAILURE_MODES: INVALID_COUNT
  DATA_TRANSITION: empty list -> list of length count
  TERMINATION: total
  unit-testable: yes

procedure GENERATE_FIBONACCI_SEQUENCE(count):
  # [IMPL-FIBONACCI_GENERATE_SEQUENCE] [ARCH-FIBONACCI_CLI_SCRIPT] [REQ-FIBONACCI_PRINT] How: Return the first count terms of the zero-based Fibonacci sequence as an integer list.
  1. IF count < 0:
       RETURN error INVALID_COUNT
  2. IF count == 0:
       RETURN []
  3. IF count == 1:
       RETURN [0]
  4. SET sequence = [0, 1]
  5. WHILE length(sequence) < count:
       SET next_term = last(sequence) + second_last(sequence)
       APPEND next_term to sequence
  6. RETURN sequence
